msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-pages.php:678
msgid "Where the canonical of a filter page with exactly one term points. \"Term archive\": the category, tag or custom taxonomy archive of that term, which shows the same posts - as long as that archive is public, lists this post type and is not set to noindex in Rank Math or Yoast; otherwise the filter URL. \"Filter URL\": the filter page itself. \"Off\": no canonical at all, also none from Rank Math or Yoast. Paginated pages always point to page 1."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-pages.php:690
msgid "Archive base (recommended)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-pages.php:695
msgid "Where the canonical of a filter page with two or more terms points. \"Archive base\": the unfiltered blog page or post type archive, as long as it is not set to noindex in Rank Math or Yoast; this replaces the noindex of these pages (they stay nofollow). Otherwise, and with \"Filter URL\", the page follows \"Indexable Filter Pages\" as before. \"Off\": no canonical at all, also none from Rank Math or Yoast. With the default robots.txt rules, combinations within one group stay blocked, so crawlers never see their canonical."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-pages.php:718
msgid "Maximum number of selected terms across all filter groups together. The filter bar disables further terms once it is reached, and the server rejects longer combinations. 0 = no limit."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-pages.php:729
msgid "Redirect and reject filter URLs before the database is queried"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-pages.php:731
msgid "Every other spelling of a selection (term order, duplicates, upper case, /page/1/) is redirected (301) to its one canonical address. Combinations beyond the limits above, and extra URL segments, are rejected with a short error page. Without this, every variant is rendered as a full page."
msgstr ""

